IMPORT prelude

-- Diplomatic and Consular Relations Act 2005 (Singapore) -- who in a foreign embassy or consulate can be sued, prosecuted, arrested,
-- made to give evidence or taxed in Singapore, and what waives or ends that; when police may enter their premises; a consular
-- officer's powers over a deceased national's estate; and the Minister's conclusive certificate. Sections 3, 4, 5, 7 and the
-- Articles of the Vienna Conventions (First and Second Schedules) that those sections give the force of law: VCDR Arts 22, 29, 30,
-- 31, 32, 33, 34, 37, 38, 39; VCCR Arts 31(2), 41, 43, 44, 45, 49, 53, 57(2), 58(2)-(3), 66, 71.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DCRA2005.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the retrieval
-- metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026. The only amendment annotated in the text is [27/2014] (s 5(9));
-- the Legislative History lists Act 27 of 2014 (Family Justice Act 2014, s 55, in force 1 January 2015) as the last amending Act.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0141 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For an ordinary person or business the Act matters when the other party -- a tenant, a debtor, a driver, an
-- employer, an heir's representative -- belongs to a foreign mission or consulate. SCOPED to that.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Minister's reciprocity orders withdrawing or extending privileges (s 6) except as a caveat; regulations (s 8);
-- inviolability of archives, bags, correspondence and couriers (VCDR 24, 27; VCCR 33, 35); customs and baggage (VCDR 36; VCCR 50);
-- premises taxes (VCDR 23; VCCR 32, 60); personal services (VCDR 35; VCCR 52, 67); third-State transit (VCDR 40; VCCR 54); estate duty
-- on a deceased member's movables (VCDR 39(4); VCCR 51); the honorary consular post regime beyond Arts 58 and 66; the family of
-- administrative and technical staff (Art 37(2)) as a separate role. Whether a person is a "diplomatic agent", a member of a household,
-- or "permanently resident" is taken as given: the Act does not define permanent residence.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Diplomatic and Consular Relations Act 2005 -- privileges and immunities`

-- VCDR Art 1: a "diplomatic agent" is "the head of the mission or a member of the diplomatic staff"; the staff are also
-- "administrative and technical staff" and "service staff" ("domestic service of the mission"); a "private servant" is "in the domestic
-- service of a member of the mission and ... not an employee of the sending State". VCCR Art 1: "consular officer", "consular employee"
-- (administrative or technical service), "member of the service staff" (domestic service of the post); Art 1(2): career and honorary
-- consular officers.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `diplomatic agent`
    `family member of a diplomatic agent`
    `administrative and technical staff of a mission`
    `service staff of a mission`
    `private servant of a mission member`
    `career consular officer`
    `honorary consular officer`
    `consular employee`
    `service staff of a consular post`
    `family member of a career consular officer`

-- s 3(2)(b), s 4(2)(c): "a reference to a national of the receiving State is a reference to a citizen of Singapore".
DECLARE Person HAS
    `role` IS A Role
    `is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is permanently resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the member` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is local` IF
        `the member`'s `is a Singapore citizen`
    OR  `the member`'s `is permanently resident in Singapore`

DECLARE Subject IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary matter`
    `private immovable property in Singapore`
    `a succession as a private person`
    `private professional or commercial activity`
    `a contract not made as agent of the sending State`
    `a third-party claim for a vehicle, vessel or aircraft accident`

DECLARE Proceedings HAS
    `criminal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `about an act in the course of official functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `subject` IS A Subject

§§ `s 3(1), VCDR Arts 31, 37, 38 -- immunity of mission members`

-- s 3(1): "Articles 1, 22, 23, 24 and 27 to 40 of the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations have the force of law in Singapore."
-- Art 31(1): a diplomatic agent "shall enjoy immunity from the criminal jurisdiction" and from civil and administrative jurisdiction
-- "except in the case of: (a) a real action relating to private immovable property ... unless he holds it on behalf of the sending
-- State ...; (b) an action relating to succession in which the diplomatic agent is involved ... as a private person ...; (c) an
-- action relating to any professional or commercial activity ... outside his official functions."
GIVEN `the case` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Article 31(1) exception applies to` IF
        (NOT `the case`'s `criminal`)
    AND (NOT `the case`'s `about an act in the course of official functions`)
    AND CONSIDER `the case`'s `subject`
        WHEN `private immovable property in Singapore` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a succession as a private person` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `private professional or commercial activity` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the case` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-local diplomatic agent is immune from` IF
    NOT `an Article 31(1) exception applies to` `the case`

-- Art 37(1): household family of a diplomatic agent, "if they are not nationals of the receiving State", get Arts 29 to 36 -- the
-- condition names nationals only, not permanent residents. Art 37(2): administrative and technical staff, "if they are not nationals
-- of or permanently resident", get Arts 29 to 35, "except that the immunity from civil and administrative jurisdiction ... shall not
-- extend to acts performed outside the course of their duties". Art 37(3): service staff not nationals or permanent residents get
-- "immunity in respect of acts performed in the course of their duties". Art 37(4): private servants get tax exemption on emoluments
-- and otherwise privileges "only to the extent admitted by the receiving State". Art 38(1): a diplomatic agent who is a national or
-- permanent resident gets "only immunity from jurisdiction, and inviolability, in respect of official acts". Art 38(2): other staff and
-- servants who are nationals or permanent residents get privileges "only to the extent admitted by the receiving State".
--
-- VCCR Art 43(1): "Consular officers and consular employees shall not be amenable to the jurisdiction of the judicial or administrative
-- authorities ... in respect of acts performed in the exercise of consular functions." (2): not "in respect of a civil action either:
-- (a) arising out of a contract ... in which he did not contract expressly or impliedly as an agent of the sending State; or (b) by a
-- third party for damage arising from an accident in the receiving State caused by a vehicle, vessel or aircraft."
GIVEN `the case` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 43 covers` IF
        `the case`'s `about an act in the course of official functions`
    AND (    `the case`'s `criminal`
         OR  CONSIDER `the case`'s `subject`
             WHEN `a contract not made as agent of the sending State` THEN FALSE
             WHEN `a third-party claim for a vehicle, vessel or aircraft accident` THEN FALSE
             OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- Art 43 names consular officers and consular employees only; the service staff of a consular post and consular families are not in
-- it. Art 58(2) applies Art 43 to honorary consular officers. Art 57(2)(a) (in force by s 4(1), read with s 4(6)): the privileges and
-- immunities of Section II of Chapter II -- which contains Art 43 -- "shall not be accorded ... to consular employees or to members of the
-- service staff who carry on any private gainful occupation in the receiving State". Art 71(1): a consular officer who is a national
-- or permanent resident enjoys "only immunity from jurisdiction and personal inviolability in respect of official acts"; (2): other
-- local members only so far as granted. INFERENCE: a local consular officer keeps Art 43 as qualified by Art 43(2); Art 71(1) is read
-- as a ceiling, not as removing the Art 43(2) carve-outs.
-- s 5(11): no privilege or immunity for acts under s 5 or s 59 of the Probate and Administration Act 1934 (not modelled here).
GIVEN `the member` IS A Person, `the case` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is immune from the proceedings` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`'s `role`
    WHEN `diplomatic agent` THEN
        IF `the member is local` `the member`
        THEN `the case`'s `about an act in the course of official functions`
        ELSE `a non-local diplomatic agent is immune from` `the case`
    WHEN `family member of a diplomatic agent` THEN
        IF `the member`'s `is a Singapore citizen`
        THEN FALSE
        ELSE `a non-local diplomatic agent is immune from` `the case`
    WHEN `administrative and technical staff of a mission` THEN
            (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
        AND (`the case`'s `criminal` OR `the case`'s `about an act in the course of official functions`)
    WHEN `service staff of a mission` THEN
            (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
        AND `the case`'s `about an act in the course of official functions`
    WHEN `career consular officer` THEN `Article 43 covers` `the case`
    WHEN `honorary consular officer` THEN `Article 43 covers` `the case`
    WHEN `consular employee` THEN
            (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
        AND (NOT `the member`'s `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore`)
        AND `Article 43 covers` `the case`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 3(3), s 4(5), VCDR Art 32, VCCR Art 45 -- waiver`

-- VCDR Art 32(1): immunity "may be waived by the sending State"; (2) "Waiver must always be express"; (3) a person who starts
-- proceedings cannot invoke immunity "in respect of any counter-claim directly connected with the principal claim"; (4) waiver for
-- civil proceedings does not imply waiver "in respect of the execution of the judgment, for which a separate waiver shall be
-- necessary". s 3(3): a waiver by the head of the mission "is treated as a waiver by that State". VCCR Art 45(2): "express ... and
-- shall be communicated to the receiving State in writing"; s 4(5): waiver by the head of the diplomatic mission, or if none, of the
-- consular post, counts as the State's.
DECLARE Waiver IS ONE OF
    `no waiver`
    `an express written waiver by the head of mission`
    `conduct suggesting a waiver`

GIVEN `the waiver` IS A Waiver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the waiver is effective` IF
    CONSIDER `the waiver`
    WHEN `an express written waiver by the head of mission` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the member` IS A Person, `the case` IS A Proceedings, `the waiver` IS A Waiver,
      `it is a directly connected counter-claim to proceedings the member began` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may hear the case` IF
        (NOT `the member is immune from the proceedings` `the member` `the case`)
    OR  `the waiver is effective` `the waiver`
    OR  `it is a directly connected counter-claim to proceedings the member began`

-- Art 31(3): "No measures of execution may be taken ... except in the cases coming under sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)"; Art 32(4)
-- and VCCR Art 45(4): a separate waiver for execution. The inviolability of person and residence that also limits execution under
-- Art 31(3) is not modelled.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Person, `the case` IS A Proceedings, `execution was separately and expressly waived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a judgment may be enforced` IF
        (NOT `the member is immune from the proceedings` `the member` `the case`)
    OR  `execution was separately and expressly waived`

§§ `s 4(2)(b), VCDR Art 29, VCCR Art 41 -- arrest and detention`

-- s 4(2)(b): "a reference to a grave crime is a reference to any offence punishable with imprisonment for a term that may extend to 5
-- years or with a more severe sentence".
GIVEN `maximum years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER, `punishable with a more severe sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a grave crime` IF
        `maximum years of imprisonment` AT LEAST 5
    OR  `punishable with a more severe sentence`

-- VCDR Art 29: "The person of a diplomatic agent shall be inviolable. He shall not be liable to any form of arrest or detention."
-- Extended by Art 37(1) to non-national family and by Art 37(2) to non-local administrative and technical staff.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member has Article 29 inviolability` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`'s `role`
    WHEN `diplomatic agent` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    WHEN `family member of a diplomatic agent` THEN NOT `the member`'s `is a Singapore citizen`
    WHEN `administrative and technical staff of a mission` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- VCCR Art 41(1): consular officers "shall not be liable to arrest or detention pending trial, except in the case of a grave crime and
-- pursuant to a decision by the competent judicial authority"; (2) otherwise no imprisonment or restriction "save in execution of a
-- judicial decision of final effect". Art 41 is in Section II of Chapter II (career officers); Art 58(2) does NOT apply it to honorary
-- consular officers. Art 71(1): a local consular officer has personal inviolability only "in respect of official acts".
-- INFERENCE: a person immune from jurisdiction for the act (Art 37(3), Art 43, Art 38(1)) cannot be arrested for it.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Person, `the case` IS A Proceedings, `maximum years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER,
      `punishable with a more severe sentence` IS A BOOLEAN, `a competent judicial authority has so decided` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in execution of a final judicial decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may be arrested or detained` IF
    IF `the member has Article 29 inviolability` `the member`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `the member is immune from the proceedings` `the member` `the case`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE IF (`the member`'s `role` EQUALS `career consular officer`) AND (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
              THEN     `in execution of a final judicial decision`
                   OR  (    `the offence is a grave crime` `maximum years of imprisonment` `punishable with a more severe sentence`
                        AND `a competent judicial authority has so decided`)
              ELSE TRUE

§§ `VCDR Art 31(2), VCCR Arts 44, 58(2), 71 -- giving evidence`

-- VCDR Art 31(2): "A diplomatic agent is not obliged to give evidence as a witness" (extended by Art 37(1), (2)). VCCR Art 44(1): a
-- consular employee or service staff "shall not ... decline to give evidence"; "If a consular officer should decline to do so, no
-- coercive measure or penalty may be applied to him." (3): no obligation "concerning matters connected with the exercise of their
-- functions" and may decline "as expert witnesses with regard to the law of the sending State". Art 58(2) applies only paragraph 3
-- of Art 44 to honorary consular officers; Art 71(1) likewise to local consular officers. INFERENCE: a local diplomatic agent (Art
-- 38(1)) may decline only on official acts.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Person, `about matters connected with their functions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `as an expert on the law of the sending State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member can be compelled to give evidence` IF
    IF `the member has Article 29 inviolability` `the member`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the member`'s `role`
         WHEN `diplomatic agent` THEN NOT `about matters connected with their functions`
         WHEN `career consular officer` THEN
             IF `the member is local` `the member`
             THEN NOT (`about matters connected with their functions` OR `as an expert on the law of the sending State`)
             ELSE FALSE
         WHEN `honorary consular officer` THEN
             NOT (`about matters connected with their functions` OR `as an expert on the law of the sending State`)
         WHEN `consular employee` THEN
             IF `the member is local` `the member` OR `the member`'s `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore`
             THEN TRUE
             ELSE NOT (`about matters connected with their functions` OR `as an expert on the law of the sending State`)
         WHEN `service staff of a consular post` THEN
             IF `the member is local` `the member` OR `the member`'s `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore`
             THEN TRUE
             ELSE NOT (`about matters connected with their functions` OR `as an expert on the law of the sending State`)
         OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `VCDR Arts 34, 37, VCCR Arts 49, 57(2), 58(3), 66, 71 -- taxes`

-- VCDR Art 34: a diplomatic agent is exempt from all dues and taxes except "(a) indirect taxes of a kind which are normally
-- incorporated in the price of goods or services; (b) dues and taxes on private immovable property ...; (c) estate, succession or
-- inheritance duties ...; (d) dues and taxes on private income having its source in the receiving State ...; (e) charges levied for
-- specific services rendered; (f) registration, court or record fees, mortgage dues and stamp duty, with respect to immovable
-- property". VCCR Art 49(1) gives consular officers and employees AND "members of their families forming part of their households"
-- the same list (adding capital gains and duties on transfers). Art 37(3), (4): service staff and private servants (non-local) --
-- "exemption from dues and taxes on the emoluments they receive by reason of their employment". VCCR 49(2): consular service staff
-- "exempt from dues and taxes on the wages which they receive for their services". Art 66: an honorary consular officer is exempt on
-- "the remuneration and emoluments which he receives from the sending State". Art 58(3): no privileges for an honorary officer's family.
-- Art 71(1) says local consular officers "shall enjoy only" jurisdictional immunity, inviolability and Art 44(3). INFERENCE: that
-- "only" displaces Art 66 and every tax exemption for a local consular officer, honorary or career.
DECLARE Tax IS ONE OF
    `income tax on the pay of their post`
    `income tax on private Singapore-source income`
    `property tax on a private home they own in Singapore`
    `an indirect tax built into the price of goods or services`
    `stamp duty on buying private immovable property`
    `a charge for a specific service rendered`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member has the full tax exemption` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`'s `role`
    WHEN `diplomatic agent` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    WHEN `family member of a diplomatic agent` THEN NOT `the member`'s `is a Singapore citizen`
    WHEN `administrative and technical staff of a mission` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    WHEN `career consular officer` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    WHEN `consular employee` THEN
            (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
        AND (NOT `the member`'s `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore`)
    WHEN `family member of a career consular officer` THEN
            (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
        AND (NOT `the member`'s `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the member` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member has the pay-only tax exemption` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`'s `role`
    WHEN `service staff of a mission` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    WHEN `private servant of a mission member` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    WHEN `service staff of a consular post` THEN
            (NOT `the member is local` `the member`)
        AND (NOT `the member`'s `carries on a private gainful occupation in Singapore`)
    WHEN `honorary consular officer` THEN NOT `the member is local` `the member`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the member` IS A Person, `the tax` IS A Tax
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is exempt from the tax` IF
        (`the member has the full tax exemption` `the member` OR `the member has the pay-only tax exemption` `the member`)
    AND CONSIDER `the tax`
        WHEN `income tax on the pay of their post` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `VCDR Art 33(2), (3) -- social security for a diplomat's private servant`

-- Art 33(2): the social security exemption applies "to private servants who are in the sole employ of a diplomatic agent, on
-- condition: (a) that they are not nationals of or permanently resident in the receiving State; and (b) that they are covered by the
-- social security provisions ... of the sending State or a third State." (3): a diplomatic agent who employs persons to whom the
-- exemption does not apply "shall observe the obligations which the social security provisions of the receiving State impose upon
-- employers".
GIVEN `the servant` IS A Person, `in the sole employ of the diplomatic agent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `covered by the social security of the sending State or a third State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the diplomat must meet Singapore employer social security obligations for the servant` IF
    NOT (    `in the sole employ of the diplomatic agent`
         AND (NOT `the member is local` `the servant`)
         AND `covered by the social security of the sending State or a third State`)

§§ `VCDR Art 39(2), VCCR Art 53(3), (4) -- when immunity ends`

-- VCDR Art 39(2): when functions end, privileges and immunities "shall normally cease at the moment when he leaves the country, or on
-- expiry of a reasonable period in which to do so ... However, with respect to acts performed by such a person in the exercise of his
-- functions as a member of the mission, immunity shall continue to subsist." VCCR Art 53(3), (4): the same, "whichever is the
-- sooner", and immunity for official acts continues "without limitation of time". Assumes the person had immunity for the act.
GIVEN `the functions have ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `has left Singapore or had a reasonable period to leave` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act was in the exercise of functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the immunity still subsists` IF
        (NOT `the functions have ended`)
    OR  (NOT `has left Singapore or had a reasonable period to leave`)
    OR  `the act was in the exercise of functions`

§§ `s 3(2)(a), s 4(2)(a), VCDR Arts 22, 30, VCCR Arts 31(2), 58(1) -- entry by police and officials`

-- s 3(2)(a), s 4(2)(a): "agents" / "authorities" of the receiving State include "any police officer and any person exercising a power
-- of entry to any premises under any written law". VCDR Art 22(1): the premises of the mission "shall be inviolable. The agents of the
-- receiving State may not enter them, except with the consent of the head of the mission." Art 30(1): the private residence of a
-- diplomatic agent has "the same inviolability". VCCR Art 31(2) (in force; para 3 is not): authorities "shall not enter that part of
-- the consular premises which is used exclusively for the purpose of the work of the consular post except with the consent" of the
-- head of post, a designee or the head of the mission; "consent ... may, however, be assumed in case of fire or other disaster
-- requiring prompt protective action". Art 58(1) does not apply Art 31 to a post headed by an honorary consular officer. The
-- Diplomatic Convention has no fire exception.
DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `the premises of a diplomatic mission`
    `a diplomatic agent's private residence`
    `the working part of a career consular post`
    `other parts of career consular premises`
    `the premises of an honorary consular post`

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `consent given` IS A BOOLEAN, `fire or other disaster requiring prompt protective action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `officers may enter` IF
    CONSIDER `the premises`
    WHEN `the premises of a diplomatic mission` THEN `consent given`
    WHEN `a diplomatic agent's private residence` THEN `consent given`
    WHEN `the working part of a career consular post` THEN
        `consent given` OR `fire or other disaster requiring prompt protective action`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 5 -- consular officers and a deceased person's estate`

-- s 5(1): where a national of a State to which the section applies (a "relevant person") is named executor or may otherwise take a
-- grant, "a consular officer of that State has made an application", "the court is satisfied that the relevant person is not
-- resident in Singapore", and "no application ... has been made by the relevant person or by any person duly authorised under a
-- power of attorney", "the court MUST make to the consular officer such grant". (2): the court may postpone the grant. (12): the
-- section applies to a State named by Ministerial order, being one with a consular convention providing for these matters.
GIVEN `the State is named in a s 5(12) order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the national is named executor or may take a grant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the consular officer has applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `the national is not resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the national or their attorney has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must grant representation to the consular officer` IF
        `the State is named in a s 5(12) order`
    AND `the national is named executor or may take a grant`
    AND `the consular officer has applied`
    AND `the national is not resident in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the national or their attorney has applied`)

-- s 5(3), (4): where a non-resident relevant person is entitled to money or property from an estate or due on a death, the consular
-- officer "has the like right and power to receive and give a valid discharge ... as if ... duly authorised by a power of attorney".
-- (5): "no person is authorised or required ... to pay or deliver any money or property to a consular officer if the person has
-- knowledge that any other person in Singapore has been expressly authorised to receive" it.
GIVEN `the State is named in a s 5(12) order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the national is not resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the national is entitled to the money or property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the payer knows someone in Singapore is expressly authorised to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payer may pay the consular officer under s 5(4)` IF
        `the State is named in a s 5(12) order`
    AND `the national is not resident in Singapore`
    AND `the national is entitled to the money or property`
    AND (NOT `the payer knows someone in Singapore is expressly authorised to receive it`)

§§ `s 7 -- the Minister's certificate`

-- s 7: "A certificate issued by or on behalf of the Minister is conclusive evidence on any question whether any person is entitled to
-- any privilege or immunity under this Act." (s 6(1)-(3) orders may also withdraw or extend privileges; not modelled.)
GIVEN `a Minister's certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN, `the certificate says the person is entitled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `entitled on the text` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is treated as entitled` IF
    IF `a Minister's certificate was issued`
    THEN `the certificate says the person is entitled`
    ELSE `entitled on the text`
